# Developer Experience (DX)

**One command** brings up a coherent environment: `make setup ENV=local|test|production`.

## Behavior matrix

| `ENV` | Brings up | Runs migrations | Seeds | Applies to |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `local` | full dev stack (api, worker, beat, postgres, redis, mailhog) via `docker-compose.yml` | yes (against dev DB) | optional (`scripts/seed_dev_data.py`) | developer machines |
| `test` | isolated test infra (postgres_test, redis_test, mailhog) via `docker-compose.test.yml` | yes (against test DB) | no — tests use factories/seeders | local & CI |
| `production` (with `SERVICE_ROLE=web|worker|beat`) | nothing (managed services on Render) | only when `SERVICE_ROLE=web` AND first replica (handled by Render `preDeployCommand`) | no | container entrypoint on Render |

## Hard rules

- ❌ NEVER add a setup path that bypasses `make setup`. README must point at it.
- ❌ NEVER read env files outside `app/core/config.py` and `scripts/setup_env.sh`.
- ❌ NEVER let `ENV=local` and `ENV=test` share volumes — separate compose files, separate volume names.
- ✅ `scripts/setup_env.sh` is idempotent: re-running with the same `ENV` is safe and fast.
- ✅ Every Make target is `.PHONY`; no implicit file deps.
- ✅ Exit codes: 0 success, non-zero on failure. CI relies on this.

## Required Make targets

| Target | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make setup ENV=...` | Delegates to `scripts/setup_env.sh "$ENV"`. |
| `make up` / `make down` | Start / stop the dev compose stack. |
| `make logs SERVICE=...` | Tail logs for a compose service. |
| `make shell` | `docker compose exec api bash`. |
| `make migrate` | `alembic upgrade head`. |
| `make migrate-down` | `alembic downgrade -1`. |
| `make migration m="<msg>"` | `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<msg>"`. |
| `make test` | Full test suite with `.env.test`. Asserts test stack is up first. |
| `make test-unit` / `make test-int` / `make test-api` | Marker-filtered runs. |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Ruff + Black. |
| `make typecheck` | Mypy strict. |
| `make precommit-install` | `pre-commit install --hook-type pre-commit --hook-type commit-msg`. |
| `make openapi` | Export `openapi.json` for diffing. |
| `make seed` | Run `scripts/seed_dev_data.py` against the dev DB. |
| `make check-env` | Verify every Settings field has an entry in `.env.example`. |
| `make security-scan` | Bandit + pip-audit + detect-secrets. |
| `make i18n-extract` | `pybabel extract -F babel.cfg -o app/locales/messages.pot app/`. |
| `make i18n-update` | `pybabel update -i app/locales/messages.pot -d app/locales/`. |
| `make i18n-compile` | `pybabel compile -d app/locales/` (.po → .mo). |
| `make i18n-check` | CI gate: completeness ≥ `LOCALE_TRANSLATION_COMPLETENESS_MIN` for every locale, no `messages.pot` drift, all catalogs compile. |
| `make new-locale L=xx` | Scaffold `app/locales/xx/LC_MESSAGES/` and `app/templates/email/<*>/xx/` stubs. |

## scripts/setup_env.sh (canonical contract)

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
ENV="${1:-local}"
case "$ENV" in
  local)
    [[ -f .env ]] || cp .env.example .env
    docker compose up -d postgres redis mailhog
    docker compose run --rm api alembic upgrade head
    docker compose run --rm api pybabel compile -d app/locales/    # ensure .mo files exist
    docker compose up -d api worker beat
    ;;
  test)
    docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml up -d
    docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml exec -T postgres_test pg_isready -t 30
    ENV_FILE=".env.test" alembic upgrade head
    pybabel compile -d app/locales/                                # tests need compiled catalogs
    ;;
  production)
    [[ -n "${SERVICE_ROLE:-}" ]] || { echo "SERVICE_ROLE is required"; exit 1; }
    exec docker/entrypoint.sh
    ;;
  *) echo "Unknown ENV: $ENV" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
```

## DX expectations

- Fresh `git clone` → `make setup ENV=local` → working API in **< 5 minutes**.
- Adding a new env var: update `Settings` + `.env.example` + (if test-relevant) `.env.test` in the same PR. CI fails on drift.
- VS Code workspace settings ship with: Black format on save, Ruff on save, mypy import resolution.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ A `Makefile.dev` and a `Makefile.prod` — one Makefile, one entry.
- ❌ A "first run" `bootstrap.sh` plus a different "daily" command — re-runnable `make setup` does both.
- ❌ Hidden side-effects (downloading models, fetching keys) in `make setup` without explicit logs.
